# Cell from playpick: mode=menus, view=820x1180,touch, save=carried.
#
# Checked direction.md first: the settings screen's seven-button CAMERA row
# (FAR/BACK/MID/IN/OVER/TAUT/FACE, src/render/theme.ts's ZOOM_NAMES) has been
# measured for size three separate times (under44 hits at three different
# viewports) but grepping every .play file in playtest/plans for "tap camera"
# turns up nothing -- no session has ever actually pressed a zoom level and
# watched what it does. src/render/theme.ts says the setting multiplies the
# fitted arena radius the live camera uses, and the SETTINGS screen's own
# BACKDROP ("a real fight, running itself behind the menus") is rendered
# through that same camera, so cycling the row should be visible without even
# leaving the settings screen -- and then should carry into a real pull.
#
# #273 is open (carried behaves as fresh across separate playbot invocations,
# PID-derived port), so this stays inside one invocation throughout.

open
tap settings
targets
shot settings-default

tap camera:0
shot settings-far
note camera level 0 (FAR), backdrop behind settings

tap camera:6
shot settings-face
note camera level 6 (FACE), backdrop behind settings

tap camera:3
shot settings-mid
note camera level 3 (IN), back to roughly the default

tap back
